---
source: crates/leptoskit_db_macros/src/tests.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\")"
---
no table: name the table the shape reads: #[db(from = User)]
unknown shape option: unknown shape option; expected `from = Table`, `public`, or `crate`
generic: a shape can't be generic
enum: a shape is a struct with a field for each value it reads
tuple: a shape needs named fields: one per value it reads
empty: a shape reads at least one value
too many fields: a shape reads at most 100 values; nest some in another shape
unknown field option: unknown shape field option; expected `column = field`, `count(link)`, `via = link`, `filter = |row| …`, `order_by = |row| …`, `limit`, `offset`, or `with_deleted`
two sources: a field reads one thing: a column, `count(…)`, or `via = …`
filter on a column: `filter`, `order_by`, `limit`, `offset`, and `with_deleted` choose linked rows; this field reads a column
order on a count: a count takes `filter`, but not `order_by`, `limit`, or `offset`
narrowing a required row: a required nested row is the one its link points at; to narrow, order, or skip rows, make the field an `Option` or a `Vec`
two tables: a shape reads one table; `from` is given twice
two limits: `limit` is given twice
limit on an option: an `Option` holds the first row; `limit` is for a `Vec`
